So, in the time it takes Petya to run 60 meters, Vasya runs 51 meters. Therefore, the time taken by Petya to run 60 meters is t = 60 / v_p. In that same time, Vasya runs 51 meters, so 51 = v_v * t = v_v * (60 / v_p). Therefore, 51 / 60 = v_v / v_p. Simplifying, that's 17/20 = v_v / v_p. Therefore, the ratio of Vasya's speed to Petya's speed is 17:20
